{"audit_run_id":"audit:1bdda2c7a1564fadbf615f4af6a0e3cd","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":70,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"*From the practice feeding-study group. Methods appendix at the end.*"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Hay is the whole diet argument in guinea pig medicine. We keep telling owners it"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"has to be the bulk of the bowl, and owners keep telling us their pig ignores the"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"rack and scatters it across the hutch. Compressed forage blocks are marketed as"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"the tidy answer. We wanted to know whether the animal chewing that block is"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"doing the same dental work as the animal pulling long stems off a rack."},{"end_column":78,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"Thirty-four adult guinea pigs, each from a different household, took part for"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"eight weeks. Seventeen were fed long-stem hay from an open rack, seventeen were"},{"end_column":73,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"fed the same hay compressed into forage blocks. Nothing else in the diet"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"differed. At the end of the eight weeks every animal was weighed, examined under"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"sedation, and had two days of intake and output recorded at home by its owner on"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"scales we supplied."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"The analysis reads one file, `guinea_pig_hay_study.csv`. **One row is one guinea"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"pig**: a single adult animal from a single household, carrying its feeding"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"treatment and its six end-of-study measurements. Each animal appears exactly"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"once, and every animal has a value in every column, so there are no blanks. The"},{"end_column":62,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"file holds 34 data rows plus a header row, and eight columns."},{"end_column":34,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| Column | Unit | What it holds |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":114,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `animal_id` | none (text label) | Study identifier for the animal, `GP01` through `GP34`. Unique across rows. |"},{"end_column":211,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"| `group` | none (text label) | Feeding treatment, with exactly two possible entries: `hay_rack` (long-stem hay from an open rack) and `forage_block` (the same hay compressed into blocks). 17 animals in each. |"},{"end_column":107,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"| `hay_intake_g_day` | grams per day | Daily hay dry matter intake, averaged over the two recorded days. |"},{"end_column":103,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"| `body_weight_g` | grams | Body weight at the end of the eight weeks, from the sedated examination. |"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"| `faecal_output_g_day` | grams per day | Daily faecal output, averaged over the two recorded days. |"},{"end_column":122,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"| `faecal_particle_mm` | millimetres | Median faecal particle size, our marker of how finely the animal chewed its hay. |"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"| `chewing_min_day` | minutes per day | Time spent chewing, scored from video of one recorded day. |"},{"end_column":104,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"| `occlusal_angle_deg` | degrees | Cheek tooth occlusal angle, measured on the intraoral photographs. |"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"The six outcome columns appear in the order the protocol declared them, and the"},{"end_column":47,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"results below are reported in that same order."},{"end_column":78,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"Each of the six outcomes was declared as a question in its own right, so each"},{"end_column":68,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"one gets its own answer at the conventional five percent threshold."},{"end_column":80,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"**1. Daily hay dry matter intake (g/day).** Hay rack 56.14, forage block 55.42,"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"a difference of 0.72 g/day. p = 0.84. The two groups ate essentially the same"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"amount of hay."},{"end_column":78,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"**2. End-of-study body weight (g).** Hay rack 960.18, forage block 1003.94, a"},{"end_column":74,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"difference of -43.76 g. p = 0.39. No detectable weight difference between"},{"end_column":15,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"presentations."},{"end_column":74,"end_line":53,"start_column":1,"start_line":53,"text":"**3. Daily faecal output (g/day).** Hay rack 43.15, forage block 44.11, a"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"difference of -0.96 g/day. p = 0.74. What went in came out at the same rate in"},{"end_column":50,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"both groups, which fits the matched intake above."},{"end_column":77,"end_line":57,"start_column":1,"start_line":57,"text":"**4. Median faecal particle size (mm).** Hay rack 0.81, forage block 1.16, a"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":58,"start_column":1,"start_line":58,"text":"difference of -0.35 mm. p = 0.0000055. Block-fed animals passed noticeably"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"coarser particles, so they were breaking the hay down less finely."},{"end_column":75,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"**5. Time spent chewing per day (min/day).** Hay rack 205.65, forage block"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"160.76, a difference of 44.88 minutes. p = 0.00015. Rack-fed animals spent"},{"end_column":72,"end_line":63,"start_column":1,"start_line":63,"text":"roughly three quarters of an hour more per day with their jaws working."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"**6. Cheek tooth occlusal angle (degrees).** Hay rack 30.01, forage block 32.38,"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"a difference of -2.37 degrees. p = 0.047. The block-fed animals sat at a steeper"},{"end_column":64,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"occlusal angle, the direction we associate with less even wear."},{"end_column":80,"end_line":71,"start_column":1,"start_line":71,"text":"Hay presentation did not change how much the animals ate, what they weighed, or"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"how much they passed. Intake, weight and output came out flat across the two"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"groups. The differences were all in *how* the hay was processed and what that"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"did to the teeth: block-fed pigs chewed about 45 minutes less per day, passed"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"coarser faecal particles, and finished the eight weeks with a steeper cheek"},{"end_column":22,"end_line":76,"start_column":1,"start_line":76,"text":"tooth occlusal angle."},{"end_column":76,"end_line":78,"start_column":1,"start_line":78,"text":"Practical advice for owners: forage blocks are a reasonable way to keep hay"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":79,"start_column":1,"start_line":79,"text":"intake up and the hutch tidy, but they are not a substitute for long-stem hay"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":80,"start_column":1,"start_line":80,"text":"when it comes to dental wear. Where an animal is on blocks, we suggest keeping a"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":81,"start_column":1,"start_line":81,"text":"rack of long-stem hay available alongside it, and we would not present blocks as"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":82,"start_column":1,"start_line":82,"text":"the only hay source in a pig with any existing cheek tooth abnormality. The"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":83,"start_column":1,"start_line":83,"text":"weight and output results are reassuring, so an owner switching for practical"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":84,"start_column":1,"start_line":84,"text":"reasons is not risking condition; the trade-off is chewing time, not nutrition."},{"end_column":75,"end_line":86,"start_column":1,"start_line":86,"text":"Two honest limits. The occlusal angle result sits just under the threshold"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":87,"start_column":1,"start_line":87,"text":"(p = 0.047), so it is the weakest of the three findings and would want repeating"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":88,"start_column":1,"start_line":88,"text":"in a larger group before we lean on it hard. And eight weeks is short next to"},{"end_column":60,"end_line":89,"start_column":1,"start_line":89,"text":"the years over which cheek tooth problems actually develop."},{"end_column":4,"end_line":91,"start_column":1,"start_line":91,"text":"---"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":95,"start_column":1,"start_line":95,"text":"**Design.** Thirty-four adult guinea pigs, one per household, allocated 17 to"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":96,"start_column":1,"start_line":96,"text":"long-stem hay from an open rack and 17 to compressed forage blocks, fed for"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":97,"start_column":1,"start_line":97,"text":"eight weeks. Six outcomes measured on every animal at the end of the study, in"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":98,"start_column":1,"start_line":98,"text":"the protocol's declared order: daily hay dry matter intake, end-of-study body"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":99,"start_column":1,"start_line":99,"text":"weight, daily faecal output, median faecal particle size, daily chewing time"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":100,"start_column":1,"start_line":100,"text":"from video scoring of one recorded day, and cheek tooth occlusal angle from"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":101,"start_column":1,"start_line":101,"text":"intraoral photographs. Intake and output are the mean of two owner-recorded"},{"end_column":6,"end_line":102,"start_column":1,"start_line":102,"text":"days."},{"end_column":79,"end_line":104,"start_column":1,"start_line":104,"text":"**Analysis.** Each declared outcome was analysed separately. For every outcome"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":105,"start_column":1,"start_line":105,"text":"the two feeding treatments were compared with a two-sample (Welch) t-test on the"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":106,"start_column":1,"start_line":106,"text":"34 animal values, and the outcome was called significant at the conventional"},{"end_column":74,"end_line":107,"start_column":1,"start_line":107,"text":"five percent threshold (alpha = 0.05). The animal is the unit of analysis"},{"end_column":63,"end_line":108,"start_column":1,"start_line":108,"text":"throughout, and each animal contributes one value per outcome."},{"end_column":80,"end_line":110,"start_column":1,"start_line":110,"text":"**No multiple-comparison adjustment was applied.** Each of the six outcomes was"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":111,"start_column":1,"start_line":111,"text":"declared in the protocol as a question in its own right and carries its own"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":112,"start_column":1,"start_line":112,"text":"conclusion at the conventional threshold, so the p-values above are unadjusted."},{"end_column":77,"end_line":114,"start_column":1,"start_line":114,"text":"**Software.** The analysis is a single script, `analysis.py`, in the project"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":115,"start_column":1,"start_line":115,"text":"root. It reads `guinea_pig_hay_study.csv`, builds one collection of per-outcome"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":116,"start_column":1,"start_line":116,"text":"results in a single pass over the declared outcome list, and prints the two"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":117,"start_column":1,"start_line":117,"text":"treatment means, the difference and the p-value for each outcome in the declared"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":118,"start_column":1,"start_line":118,"text":"order. It uses pandas for the table and `scipy.stats.ttest_ind` (with"},{"end_column":73,"end_line":119,"start_column":1,"start_line":119,"text":"`equal_var=False`) for the comparison. Run it from the project root with"},{"end_column":22,"end_line":120,"start_column":1,"start_line":120,"text":"`python analysis.py`."},{"end_column":48,"end_line":122,"start_column":1,"start_line":122,"text":"**Full result table as printed by the script:**"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":124,"start_column":1,"start_line":124,"text":"| Outcome | Unit | Mean rack | Mean block | Difference | p-value | Result |"},{"end_column":48,"end_line":125,"start_column":1,"start_line":125,"text":"| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":126,"start_column":1,"start_line":126,"text":"| Daily hay dry matter intake | g/day | 56.14 | 55.42 | 0.72 | 0.8415 | not significant |"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":127,"start_column":1,"start_line":127,"text":"| End-of-study body weight | g | 960.18 | 1003.94 | -43.76 | 0.3876 | not significant |"},{"end_column":83,"end_line":128,"start_column":1,"start_line":128,"text":"| Daily faecal output | g/day | 43.15 | 44.11 | -0.96 | 0.7385 | not significant |"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":129,"start_column":1,"start_line":129,"text":"| Median faecal particle size | mm | 0.81 | 1.16 | -0.35 | 0.0000055 | significant |"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":130,"start_column":1,"start_line":130,"text":"| Time spent chewing per day | min/day | 205.65 | 160.76 | 44.88 | 0.00015 | significant |"},{"end_column":84,"end_line":131,"start_column":1,"start_line":131,"text":"| Cheek tooth occlusal angle | deg | 30.01 | 32.38 | -2.37 | 0.0470 | significant |"},{"end_column":61,"end_line":133,"start_column":1,"start_line":133,"text":"Difference is the hay rack mean minus the forage block mean."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:d2324427bbf446607ec3","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:6cd9983aff9bd16bd2e84b97befd3f5ac00cd83ea2a0998f47d2ea6144b7e94c","end_line":133,"locator":"report.md:1-133","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
